(:taskCollection
  :id "Phase447CanonicalLexiconCrossClient"
  :createdAt 1789142884943
  :status "done"
  :priorityOrder 11
  :summary "Canonical Lexicon Cross-Client: one spoken-to-canonical source rendered to every client and both translators, the mishearing retired from artifact names, and a checker so it cannot return."
  :phase "Phase447CanonicalLexiconCrossClient"
  :baseline "2026-09-11: voice/src/hyness_profile.asl:51 maps хайнесс to hyness instead of harness; the owner confirmed 2026-09-12 that harness is also heard as ханес, so a term carries several spoken forms and a single-form table cannot hold them; the mishearing occurs 78 times across five files and names the module, three structs, the profile value and .asl/hyness.config.asn; the alias table holds five entries, is imported by one test only, and is invisible to prompt_translator, to AGENTS.md and to every client channel."
  :tasks [
    (:task
      :id "Task44701"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-447"
      :title "Canonical lexicon as a single source, rendered to every client"
      :kind :protocol
      :lane "lexicon"
      :state :done
      :priority :critical
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789142884943
      :updatedAt 1789430100000
      :motivation "Measured 2026-09-11: voice/src/hyness_profile.asl:51 maps the spoken form хайнесс to hyness rather than to harness, so the table that exists to correct a mishearing instead records it as the target. The table lives inside the voice package, is imported only by one test, and is invisible to prompt_translator, to AGENTS.md and to every client channel, so a term dictated into Claude Code, Codex or Antigravity is never corrected at all. Five aliases are declared and only the terms spoken aloud during a voice session can benefit."
      :purpose "asl/grammar/lexicon.asn is the single source of spoken-to-canonical mappings with camelCase keys: each entry carries :spoken forms (several per term), :canonical, :scope (project, tool, person, path) and :why. scripts/install.sh --render-lexicon projects it into every client channel and into the voice and prompt translators, exactly as rules are projected; --check-lexicon exits 1 on divergence. A canonical value that is itself a mishearing fails the gate."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["asl/grammar/lexicon.asn with multiple spoken forms per term" "Rendered into every client channel and both translators" "--check-lexicon gates divergence" "хайнесс maps to harness"]
      :owns ["asl/grammar/lexicon.asn" "scripts/install.sh" "AGENTS.md" "asl/asl"]
      :targetSymbols ["rules_main" "render_between"]
      :relatedSymbols ["ssot" "names" "output"]
      :invariants ["C5" "D51" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task43707"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44701"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task44701.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A spoken form rendering to a different canonical value in two surfaces fails the check; a canonical value equal to a known mishearing fails." "A term added to the lexicon appears in every client channel after one render, with no per-client table remaining."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44701" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [(:receipt :taskId "Task44701" :passed true :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44701" :assertCount 27 :at 1789430100000)]
      :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Verifier fixes spoken forms with known canonical targets." "Author the lexicon from the voice table plus the terms observed in session transcripts." "Extend the renderer with a lexicon surface." "Add --check-lexicon." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 1
      :receipts [(:receipt :step 1 :status :ok :hash "HEAD")])
    (:task
      :id "Task44702"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-447"
      :title "Retire the mishearing from artifact names: hyness becomes harness"
      :kind :protocol
      :lane "lexicon"
      :state :planned
      :priority :high
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789142884943
      :updatedAt 1789142884943
      :motivation "The mishearing did not stay in the dictionary: 78 occurrences across five files name the module asl-voice/hyness-profile, the structs HynessPhoneticAlias, HynessHardwareEndpoint and HynessProfile, the config .asl/hyness.config.asn and the profile value hyness-workstation. An artifact named after an ASR error teaches every future reader and every model that the error is the term."
      :purpose "Rename the module, structs, file and config to the canonical harness form with CamelCase per D51 (HarnessPhoneticAlias, HarnessHardwareEndpoint, HarnessProfile, voice/src/harness_profile.asl, .asl/harness.config.asn), update the grammar registry and the one importing test, and record the rename mapping so an older config is still readable. No occurrence of the mishearing survives outside that mapping."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Module, structs, file and config renamed" "Grammar registry updated" "Rename mapping recorded for older configs" "Zero surviving occurrences outside the mapping"]
      :owns ["voice/src/hyness_profile.asl" "voice/tests/audio_bridge_test.asl" ".asl/hyness.config.asn" "voice/grammar.asn" ".asl/mem/tasks/backlog.asn"]
      :targetSymbols ["HynessProfile" "HynessPhoneticAlias" "make-phonetic-alias"]
      :relatedSymbols ["names" "ssot" "concepts"]
      :invariants ["C5" "D51" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task44701"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44702"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task44702.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A repository-wide search for the mishearing returns only the recorded rename mapping; the renamed module still loads and its test passes." "An older config naming the previous key is read through the mapping rather than rejected."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44702" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts []
      :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Verifier fixes the expected symbol and file names." "Rename symbols and files." "Update grammar and the importing test." "Record the mapping." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 0
      :receipts [])
    (:task
      :id "Task44703"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-447"
      :title "One table, three consumers: voice transliterator, prompt translator, client channels"
      :kind :protocol
      :lane "lexicon"
      :state :planned
      :priority :high
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789142884943
      :updatedAt 1789142884943
      :motivation "Correction today happens in at most one place and only for dictated audio. The same term arrives mistyped or ASR-mangled through a pasted prompt, a Codex instruction and an Antigravity channel, and each path has either its own table or none. Three consumers with three tables is the divergence pattern the ssot rule exists to prevent."
      :purpose "voice/src/transliterator.asl and harness/src/prompt_translator.asl both consume the rendered lexicon rather than holding their own table, and every client channel carries the rendered mapping so a term is corrected before the model reasons about it. Correction is reported, not silent: a substitution emits a record naming the spoken form and the canonical value."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Both translators consume the rendered lexicon" "Client channels carry the mapping" "Substitutions are reported, never silent" "No local alias table survives"]
      :owns ["voice/src/transliterator.asl" "harness/src/prompt_translator.asl" "asl/asl"]
      :targetSymbols ["translate-prompt" "heard-name"]
      :relatedSymbols ["ssot" "output" "anchor"]
      :invariants ["C5" "D51" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task44701" "Task44702"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44703"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task44703.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["The same mangled term arriving by voice, by pasted text and by a client channel resolves to one canonical value; a substitution is visible in the trace." "Removing the local tables does not change any resolution result."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44703" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts []
      :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Verifier fixes inputs mangled through each path." "Point both translators at the rendered lexicon." "Carry the mapping into client channels." "Emit a substitution record." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 0
      :receipts [])
    (:task
      :id "Task44704"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-447"
      :title "Lexicon checker: no orphan alias, no local table, no mishearing in artifacts"
      :kind :protocol
      :lane "lexicon"
      :state :planned
      :priority :medium
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789142884943
      :updatedAt 1789142884943
      :motivation "Without a checker the lexicon will drift exactly as the rules did before ssot: a term corrected in one surface, a new local table added for convenience, a mishearing entering a filename again."
      :purpose "A static checker reports: any spoken-to-canonical pair present in one rendered surface and absent from another; any alias table outside asl/grammar/lexicon.asn; any identifier, filename or ASN key matching a known spoken form rather than its canonical value; any lexicon entry whose canonical value does not appear anywhere in the repository, which catches a canonical that is itself wrong."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Divergence across surfaces reported" "Local alias tables reported" "Spoken form appearing as an artifact name reported" "Canonical value with no referent reported"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c" "asl/packages/asl-gates/src"]
      :targetSymbols ["run_gate_6" "run_gate_7"]
      :relatedSymbols ["ssot" "names" "concepts" "capabilities"]
      :invariants ["C5" "D51" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task44703" "Task44502"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44704"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task44704.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A spoken form used as a module name is reported with both the form and its canonical value; a second alias table is reported with its path." "A lexicon entry whose canonical value appears nowhere in the repository is reported as unreferenced, catching a wrong canonical before it spreads."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44704" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts []
      :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Verifier plants each of the four violations." "Implement the four reports." "Wire into gate 6 or 7." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 0
      :receipts [])
  ])